md=['# My Recipe Book',str(recipe_count)+' selected recipes. Updated November 4, 2026.','## Contents']
for r in recipes: md.append('- '+r['title'])
for r in recipes:
    md += ['','## '+r['title'],r['yield_text'],r.get('collection','Original selections'),'','### Ingredients',*['- '+i for i in r['ingredients']],'','### Method',*[str(i+1)+'. '+s for i,s in enumerate(r['steps'])],r['notes'],'','### Nutrition',r['nutrition']]
(root/'Recipe-Book.md').write_text('\n'.join(md))
(root/'README.md').write_text('''# My Recipe Book

Self-contained searchable recipe website. No build step, accounts, analytics or external dependencies.

## Publish on GitHub Pages
Upload index.html and .nojekyll to a repository. Under Settings → Pages, select Deploy from a branch, main, / (root), then Save. The actual site URL appears there after deployment.

## Update
Edit recipes.json, then run python3 build.py after updating its recipes list (the build script currently owns the collection). Commit the regenerated index.html and Recipe-Book.md together. The Markdown companion can be imported into Google Docs; no Google Doc has been created or connected yet. There is no automatic Google Docs sync.

## Content status
16 recipes selected by the owner; nine belong to Recipes on rotation. Incomplete original details are visibly marked. Cooking steps are concise summaries, not verbatim transcripts. Earlier nutrition estimates have not been recalculated.
''')
